@* The site root, owned by the shell rather than by each host, so a host gets a working "/" without
   writing a page of its own. What it renders is the host's choice, made through AddSerginBlazorApp's
   configureHome callback; with no callback that is SerginWelcome.

   The literal "/" here is the one SerginHome.RootPath mirrors — @page templates must be literals, so the
   two spell it out separately. A host must therefore not declare its own @page "/": supplying a custom
   root is what UseComponent<T>() is for, and a second "/" template would make the routes ambiguous.

   No <PageTitle>: SerginMainLayout's fallback supplies Sergin:ApplicationName. *@

@page "/"
@inject SerginHome Home

<DynamicComponent Type="Home.ComponentType" />
